{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld","id":1515451,"title":"Magic in the Underworld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-18T03:44:51-07:00","id":1515451,"title":"Magic in the Underworld","content":"I have been thinking about the apparent lack of magic in the underworld lately. It is a realm with strong symbolic functions in which metaphysics are more important than physics, and while trying to employ the scientific method is mostly a futile endeavor, it should make a fine playground for magic instead.<br /> <br /> But we do not see that, at least, overtly. We know all splats lose their Numina after death; it is the big reset button. Mages lose their Avatar, Vampires their Disciplines (including any Blood Sorcery), even mortal Sorcerer Paths and Psychic Phenomena are gone. The only exception I know of are Mummies, who retain command of their Hekau - but they are not Wraiths, and can not learn Arcanoi. Magic itself is not banned from the realm: Workings of the rare Quick visitor or even rarer enchanted Skinlands object work just fine.<br /> <br /> This seems to indicate one of two things: Either Wraiths can not work magic, or Arcanoi <i>are</i> magic under a different name.<br /> <br /> Let's have a look at some classic magic disciplines (lower case d):<br /> <br /> <b>Astrology </b>is impossible. The sky in the Underworlds is a blank canvas with Nihils taking the place of stars. Mortal practitioners of the Starlight Path report seeing a different sky and are even able to use it for navigation. Unless a Wraith is somehow able to gain that sight, astrology is out.<br /> <br /> <b>Divination </b>on the other hand is very present. It is the bread and butter of Oracles and covered by the Fatalism Arcanos.<br /> <br /> <b>Alchemy </b>exists, but not under that name. Usurers are able to transmute Pathos, Plasm, and Corpus. Artificers and Masquers transmute Corpus via Soulforging and Moliate respectively, and the various 'elements' of the realm can exist in different phases (powdered Angst, liquid Pathos and so on), and even alloyed to achieve new properties. Alchemists (the Guild) do something similar with hardened Memories, aka Relics. Some processes, like a Usurer charging a Soulfire crystal with Pathos, might count as <b>Enchanting</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Theurgy </b>- as in: the invocation or channeling of external powers - does not seem to be a thing. The Underworld appears to be cut off well enough from whatever realms the invoked entity dwells in, and the only exception is arguably dealings with Spectres and Oblivion, which may count as a form of <b>Infernalism</b>. I will include <b>Shamanism </b>here, because Spirits of the Middle Umbra usually do not answer in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning, Binding, and Warding </b>only appear scarcely, and mostly in the context of Spectres. Harrowings might count as an example. But as with Theurgy, summoning entities from other realms seems to be impossible, or at least I'm unaware of any examples. I'm also unaware of any wards against Spectres or Whistimmu.<br /> <br /> <b>Necromancy </b>is a funny one. If there is magic in the Underworld, arguably all of it would count as Necromancy. However, it may exist as an inversion - Arcanoi dealing with the Quick, such as Embody or Puppetry, would take its place. Vivimancy?<br /> <br /> <b>Thaumaturgy </b>- as in: spell sorcery, not the specific Blood Sorcery - is the tricky one. If Arcanoi and spell sorcery are equivalent, then everything falls into this category. There is, however, one big thing missing from Arcanoi that is a staple of Thaumaturgy: Arcanoi do not have <b>Rituals</b>. As far as I know, no Arcanos has Ritual usage that results in effect beyond those of the arts.<br /> <br /> I've seen discussions on how Arcanoi may be an expression of Sphere Magick, but I'm not convinced. Functionally they more resemble Path Sorcery, but on the other hand appear to be more flexible with their alternative arts.<br /> <br /> The most interesting thing about asking whether Arcanoi and magic are equivalent - in my opinion - are the gaps that Arcanoi currently do not cover: Rituals are the big one, and I could see potential in expanding Arcanoi with a Ritual system. Formalizing Underworld alchemy is also attractive, as is tapping into Oblivion as a form of black magic for Wraiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:05:57-07:00","id":1515632,"title":"","content":"I will allow myself to bump this once, since it was stuck in spam-filter limbo and then kinda stealth-appeared.<br /> <br /> And in case the questions got lost in my ramblings: Do you think Wraith can work magic? <i>Should </i>magic exist in the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T03:04:05-07:00","id":1515640,"title":"","content":"The only official book I know of that explicitly addressed this question was the original Sorcerer, with its optional \u201cChange of Life\u201d systems (pp.54\u201356):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">A magician who dies but becomes a ghost begins as an Enfant without any of her previous Advantages. Like any other ghost, she starts out at square one with the usual traits, although her mortal abilities remain. At the Storyteller's option, The magicians mystical savvy might influence the Arcanoi she eventually masters (see sidebar); the points, however, are lost. Death is a new beginning.</span></div> According to this, sorcery is lost to wraiths. At most, it suggests a direction that the new wraith might choose to push her development of Arcanoi; but the connection isn't strong enough to warrant any kind of leg up on developing them. This is in contrast to vampires and mages, where sorcerous expertise can be converted into Spheres or Disciplines, albeit with a readjustment period: the book suggests six months or more, after which existing dots in Paths or Rituals can be converted into dots in appropriate Disciplines, or translated into freebie points that are used to acquire Arete, Spheres, or related traits. (There's also a flat prohibition against sorcerers becoming shapeshifters or changelings, which is why Gifts and Arts don't appear on the \u201cStarting Points\u201d table in that section.)<br /> <br /> So, if we take this seriously: sorcery, sphere magick, and even vampiric Disciplines can be thought of as related to each other; but Arcanoi are something entirely different, isolated from the rest. This would argue for \u201cwraiths can't learn magic\u201d and against \u201cArcanoi <i>are</i> magic\u201d. <br /> <br /> That said, the book was written at a time when the writing staff was furiously trying to put a lid on \u201ccrossover powers\u201d, due to bad experiences with the undead shapeshifting Abominations and with Samuel Haight. So take it with a grain of salt. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T03:11:32-07:00","id":1515641,"title":"","content":"Fundamentally, the Underworld is composed of memories.<br /> Wraiths are effectively memories of themselves, and they carry memories of items (in the form of relics) with them.<br /> The buildings and locations of the Shadowlands are memories of their Skinlands counterparts, and their appearance in the Shadowlands is a direct function of how they are remembered in the Skinlands - at least until enhanced using the materials of the underworld.<br /> I think the answer lies there - Wraith are... echoes of a person, and not the &quot;whole&quot; soul<br /> <br /> Parts of Being according the Egyptians (and many other cultures, but lets use the egyptians)<br /> <b>Khat</b>, the Physical Body, was often preserved to allow a smooth resurrection - obviously a Wraith don't really have this. Unless they become a Risen/Kuei-jin<br /> <b>Ba</b>, the part of the soul that ventures into the Underworld - basically the Ba is a Wraith<br /> <b>Ka</b>, the part of the soul that remains close to the body and guards it from desecration - so we already have a &quot;missing part&quot;<br /> <b>Ab</b>, the Physical Heart, the seat of consciousness - see the Khat/body above<br /> <b>Khu</b>, the physical and mystical representation of a being - basically the Aura, that ties the spiritual and material parts together. Since Wraith don't really have a body (or had one untill it rotted away, turned to dust) this one is really weak to the point of almost nonexistant. Auspex 2 descirbes the Aura colour of a Wraith &quot;Weak, intermittent aura&quot;<br /> <b>Ren</b>, the True Name, a vital part of existence and the soul, a &quot;brief&quot; summary of what the person is<br /> <b>Khaibit</b>, the Shadow, which represent the darker urges and emotions of the soul - The Shadow of a Wraith (or the Beast of a Vampire, P'o of a Kuei-jin)<br /> <b>Sahu</b>, the indestructible part of the soul that will dwell in the fields of A'aru - The Eidolon of a Wraith technically (or the Hun of a Kuei-jin. tho' the Hun more like a bit of the Ka, since it lingers around the corpse, waiting to the P'o - the Hun could be the two combined)<br /> Between these parts flows <b>Sekhem</b>, the force of life itself that binds the other soul-parts together.<br /> <br /> To preform magic, you have to be &quot;whole&quot;<br /> A Wraith of a Vampire don't have disciplines, because she is missing parts of her Being - but as soon as it became a Risen, Disciplines i na limited form, allowed, may learn Celerity, Fortitude, Obfuscate, and Potence. The Kuei-jin are a special branch of the Risen in a sense, since their creation requires every part of the being to reunite, while a &quot;common&quot; risen needs first of all a Conduit, to store and lock away its Shadow, so incomplete still - more complate than before, but still missing parts, so this limits the potential abilites<br /> <br /> Entities like the Innocent of the Mokol\u00e9 are wraiths, never been able to dream their Archid shape, but the connection to the mnesis allows them to steal, devour, corrupt or alter Memories, but themselves are while spirits in a sense, have Arcanoi<br /> <br /> I would say, as long as you are &quot;whole&quot;, you will be able to prefrom magic... any kind<br /> But after you became a Wraith, a memory, an echo what you were? Then you lost something... and either transcende, move on, or back to your body to be a Risen or Kuei-jin<br /> <br /> Magic exist in the underworld, disciplines powers and such manipulate and interract with the Underworld/Dark Umbra... in this sense Arcanoi could be consdiered &quot;magic&quot; - tho' I wouldn't consider them as such; Arcanoi are spiritual abilities that can either be taught or acquired through experience, and are aspects of a Wraith existence - in a sense, the manifestations of either the Ba or the Sekhem or both<br /> <br /> At least thisi s how I see this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T07:03:09-07:00","id":1515661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld#post1515451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Astrology </b>is impossible. The sky in the Underworlds is a blank canvas with Nihils taking the place of stars. Mortal practitioners of the Starlight Path report seeing a different sky and are even able to use it for navigation. Unless a Wraith is somehow able to gain that sight, astrology is out.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing is the Tempest sky. While in the Shadowlands the skies will certainly be darker than in the Skinlands, but the stars are still up there. Perhaps a relic telescope is all it takes to penetrate the gloom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 06-20-2023, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T12:43:42-07:00","id":1515685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515640#post1515640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At most, it suggests a direction that the new wraith might choose to push her development of Arcanoi; but the connection isn't strong enough to warrant any kind of leg up on developing them. This is in contrast to vampires and mages, where sorcerous expertise can be converted into Spheres or Disciplines</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, not being able to convert Sorcery to XP for Arcanoi would indicate <i>no</i>. I don't think vampire can cash in their Disciplines either, at least CBs Giovanni and Cappadocian do not mention it in the boxes for becoming Wraiths. I don't remember for Spheres.<br /> <br /> I think the most <i>pro</i> point I have are that Arcanoi cover a lot of ground that is traditionally covered by magic and are directly employing the metaphysics of the realm, but that is rather circumstantial.<br /> <br /> From an IC perspective, any Mage or Sorcerer who became a Wraith and whose <i>passion </i>was the exploration of arcane arts would surely pursue that goal again (after recovering from the shock of having lost it all). I don't know whether there is no mention at all of something like this means they are just out of luck, realized it through Arcanoi, or it was something never considered in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515641#post1515641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say, as long as you are &quot;whole&quot;, you will be able to prefrom magic... any kind<br /> But after you became a Wraith, a memory, an echo what you were? Then you lost something... and either transcende, move on, or back to your body to be a Risen or Kuei-jin\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I would say that Mummies - while in the Underworld\u200b - are not exactly whole, but can still use Hekau. I admittedly know too little about how Kuei and Kuei-jin work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515661#post1515661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing is the Tempest sky. While in the Shadowlands the skies will certainly be darker than in the Skinlands, but the stars are still up there. Perhaps a relic telescope is all it takes to penetrate the gloom.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I could have sworn this was also the case for the Shadowlands sky. <i>Blood Dimmed Tides</i> even has an alternative Lifeweb art for navigation (because compasses and presumably celestial navigation does not work). But maybe that was also meant for the Tempest? Although Argos is used for that.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T14:46:26-07:00","id":1515693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515685#post1515685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, not being able to convert Sorcery to XP for Arcanoi would indicate <i>no</i>. I don't think vampire can cash in their Disciplines either, at least CBs Giovanni and Cappadocian do not mention it in the boxes for becoming Wraiths. I don't remember for Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spheres to Arcanoi seems to be a no-go, too: upon death, the mage loses his Avatar and all ability to work Magick. Note that when a mage becomes a <i>vampire</i>, he loses his Spheres and doesn't get to convert them into Disciplines. I see no reason why it would be different for a mage becoming a wraith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515685#post1515685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admittedly know too little about how Kuei and Kuei-jin work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kuei-jin are treated as a vampire variant. While their \u201corigin story\u201d resembles that of a Risen (a person dies; his soul goes to something resembling an afterlife, and then it fights its way back to the body to return to a mockery of life), the devil is in the details. The \u201cafterlife\u201d they visit is more akin to DtF's Abyss than Wraith's setting \u2014 more about corruption and punishment than about death and decay \u2014 and the form they return to seems to be held together by a curse not unlike the one that allows the Kindred to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-17-2025, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T22:36:50-07:00","id":1515721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515685#post1515685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hm, I would say that Mummies - while in the Underworld\u200b - are not exactly whole, but can still use Hekau. I admittedly know too little about how Kuei and Kuei-jin work.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The Amenti whole creation is about replacing the missing part of person with the remaining part of an old mummy/someone from the Dark Kingdom of Sand, Amenti who was tore apart by the Sixth Great Maelstrom\u200b ( the Dja-akh) to create a new Dynasty member<br /> The old school mummies made by the Spell of Life &quot;preserved&quot; the Mummy<br /> <br /> In both cases, when the mummy is in the underword, their body, heart, the connection between it<i> exist</i>, as a person they are whole, while the Wraith &quot;lost something&quot; after their death<br /> At least as, I said, this is how I see it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I could be totally wrong ^^'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T00:16:19-07:00","id":1515727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515721#post1515721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could be totally wrong ^^'</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, by necessity we are speculating here. I wish there was a DA: Wraith for many reasons, but one is to see the progression and development of Arcanoi. There is a bit of a glimpse of that in the progression of Inhabit, from Kinesis during the Great War to the New Arts from the Guildbook.<br /> <br /> Back to magic, <i>Sorcerer Revised</i> discusses the option of giving linear magic to different splats (in a rather funny mega-grumpy tone, mostly because of power level concerns and redundancy). That isn't exclusive to Wraiths, but the section also mentions that they would have trouble obtaining Ritual components. Which is true, and might also serve to explain why there are no widespread Ritual uses of Arcanoi. On the other hand I do not see a particular reason why Ritual components couldn't be native, ie soulforged or plasmic. Oracles use props for their divinations, but I would describe those more as Focus items.<br /> <br /> FWIW, simply tacking on Path magic to Wraiths doesn't really feel right to me either. The 'Arcanoi as magic' option is more attractive, but the arguments against it look pretty strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T08:05:01-07:00","id":1515743,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Arcanoi, they tend to fall in to a few of categories. There are the ones like Moliate, Argos, and Castigate that manipulate things specific to the Underworld or wraithly existence. Then there are the ones like Embody or Outrage that work to reach across the Shroud. I wouldn't consider either one to be magic per se. The former is linked to the metaphysics of the world they are in and are just as likely to stem from the nature of plasm, pathos, etc. as it is to magically manipulate them. The second group maps (imperfectly) to spirit charms that accomplish similar goals.<br /> <br /> That said, there are a handful of outlier Arcanoi that point to something different. Keening, Mnemosynis, Intimation, Fatalism, etc. These all work with things that are certainly relevant to Wraiths, but are not exclusive to them or to the Underworld. We can easily make the argument that these are a kind of magic that Wraiths have tapped into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:53:53-07:00","id":1515760,"title":"","content":"Hm, good point. Maybe I have been looking at this wrong, and magic in the Underworld is about breaking or bending the 'physics' of that realm.<br /> <br /> From that point of view, charging a Soulfire crystal with Usury is less Enchanting and more like... charging your phone in the Skinlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:15:02-07:00","id":1515834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515640#post1515640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the book was written at a time when the writing staff was furiously trying to put a lid on \u201ccrossover powers\u201d, due to bad experiences with the undead shapeshifting Abominations and with Samuel Haight. So take it with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this hits the nail on the head for Wraith, apart from the isolationist setting narrative of the Shadowlands, it\u2019s the original writers not wanting to include other lore.<br /> <br /> Avoiding Uber cross-over, some of the standard lore from VTM, WTA, MTA and CTD knocks this on its head, the fact that every faction has a group that not only interacts with the shadowlands but has shared lore.<br /> <br /> If you go the whole hog there are Death Realms in the Middle Umbra and death spirits that must interact with the Shadowlands, possibly via the Tempest (so summoning, control &amp; warding has a place)<br /> <br /> So longer form ritual magic has a definitely has a place, I tend to think of it has it has to be learned or relearned once you\u2019ve died (as you do lose all living magical power upon death), it\u2019s more that the Kingdoms have suppressed or monopolised its use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld#post1515451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Necromancy </b>is a funny one. If there is magic in the Underworld, arguably all of it would count as Necromancy. However, it may exist as an inversion - Arcanoi dealing with the Quick, such as Embody or Puppetry, would take its place. Vivimancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Can really see this particularly around the Puppeteers, but also as a defence against living and unliving necromancers (if it\u2019s inverse it might well counter Necromantic control of wraiths as well as control the living, does it have some applications to the Risen as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld#post1515451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I do not see a particular reason why Ritual components couldn't be native, ie soulforged or plasmic. Oracles use props for their divinations, but I would describe those more as Focus items.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> So we have Ritual Magic specific to the Shadowlands not paths more akin to Thaumaturgic rituals or Fera Rites, called Momenti, hadn\u2019t thought of Vitomancy more grand enchantments which turn a collection of haunts into Necropoli (always felt that it had to be more to keep the maelstroms out).<br /> <br /> We also have unnatural relic plants in the shadowlands, dead forests, grave mold, traditional plants associated with death that have highly entropic patterns and manifest in the shadowlands as well as skinlands.<br /> <br /> These can be ritual components for Momenti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:16:57-07:00","id":1515836,"title":"","content":"Post trapped in Spam filter so I\u2019ll delete the duplicate when it appears<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515640#post1515640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the book was written at a time when the writing staff was furiously trying to put a lid on \u201ccrossover powers\u201d, due to bad experiences with the undead shapeshifting Abominations and with Samuel Haight. So take it with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this hits the nail on the head for Wraith, apart from the isolationist setting narrative of the Shadowlands, it\u2019s the original writers not wanting to include other lore.<br /> <br /> Avoiding Uber cross-over, some of the standard lore from VTM, WTA, MTA and CTD knocks this on its head, the fact that every faction has a group that not only interacts with the shadowlands but has shared lore.<br /> <br /> If you go the whole hog there are Death Realms in the Middle Umbra and death spirits that must interact with the Shadowlands, possibly via the Tempest (so summoning, control &amp; warding has a place)<br /> <br /> So longer form ritual magic has a definitely has a place, I tend to think of it has it has to be learned or relearned once you\u2019ve died (as you do lose all living magical power upon death), it\u2019s more that the Kingdoms have suppressed or monopolised its use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld#post1515451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Necromancy </b>is a funny one. If there is magic in the Underworld, arguably all of it would count as Necromancy. However, it may exist as an inversion - Arcanoi dealing with the Quick, such as Embody or Puppetry, would take its place. Vivimancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> Can really see this particularly around the Puppeteers, but also as a defence against living and unliving necromancers (if it\u2019s inverse it might well counter Necromantic control of wraiths as well as control the living, does it have some applications to the Risen as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld#post1515451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I do not see a particular reason why Ritual components couldn't be native, ie soulforged or plasmic. Oracles use props for their divinations, but I would describe those more as Focus items.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> So we have Ritual Magic specific to the Shadowlands not paths more akin to Thaumaturgic rituals or Fera Rites, called Momenti, hadn\u2019t thought of Vitomancy more grand enchantments which turn a collection of haunts into Necropoli (always felt that it had to be more to keep the maelstroms out).<br /> <br /> We also have unnatural relic plants in the shadowlands, dead forests, grave mold, traditional plants associated with death that have highly entropic patterns and manifest in the shadowlands as well as skinlands.<br /> <br /> These can be ritual components for Momenti.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-22-2023, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T01:38:10-07:00","id":1515934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515836#post1515836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Momenti\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this something from canon or homebrew? I don't recall seeing it before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T02:37:26-07:00","id":1515936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515934#post1515934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this something from canon or homebrew? I don't recall seeing it before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homebrew, I think inspiration came from the original VTM/WODs Society of Leopold\u2019s Theurgy and just including funerury rites in Wraith mythos.<br /> <br /> I can imagine ancient Hellenic Wraiths experimenting with Orphic rituals, later Catholism, Voudoon etc, with the concept of Fetters, Relics etc the concept of drawing power from skinlands memorial seems very in keeping with the setting.<br /> <br /> So the Ritual aspect of the Momenti is very much around drawing on Skinlands resonance/memoria.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve always sought to flesh out the Shadowlands by incorporating aspects and influences from the rest of the cosmology.<br /> <br /> Also from a KOTE perspective feels like something the Bone Flowers would teach to their Wraith allies to resist the Jade Emperor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-23-2023, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T05:10:46-07:00","id":1516002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515743#post1515743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, there are a handful of outlier Arcanoi that point to something different. Keening, Mnemosynis, Intimation, Fatalism, etc. These all work with things that are certainly relevant to Wraiths, but are not exclusive to them or to the Underworld. We can easily make the argument that these are a kind of magic that Wraiths have tapped into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still stuck on this. I've made some diagrams to see the interaction between the native 'elements' of the underworld, and even the outlier Arcanoi fit in neatly.<br /> <br /> Memory (Mnemosynis) causes Emotion (Keening) causes Passion (Intimation) causes Pathos (Usury) causes Corpus (Moliate). Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> All Arcanoi are part of this economy loop, with the Skinlands-oriented providing ways of feedback. Makes sense, since they were designed to support the game this way. Fatalism and Argos are a bit different, but fit in for the 'Journey' aspect of the soul towards Transcendence or Oblivion. I feel rather confident now to say that Arcanoi are not magic in the context of the Underworld, and perhaps are even better to use as a guideline for <i>mundane </i>effects in the Shadowlands. New Arcanoi arts therefore are more akin to scientific progression, as weird as it sounds.<br /> <br /> Any Ritual or otherwise magic would therefore exist as something separate from them, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27824_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27824\" data-vbnamecard=\"27824\">Arcanus</a> suggested. The idea for using Skinlands memoria is neat, I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T09:18:06-07:00","id":1516015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516002#post1516002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel rather confident now to say that Arcanoi are not magic in the context of the Underworld, and perhaps are even better to use as a guideline for <i>mundane </i>effects in the Shadowlands. New Arcanoi arts therefore are more akin to scientific progression, as weird as it sounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I think of it, probably how I\u2019ve always imagined Arcanoi as innate abilities drawn from the wraiths dead state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516002#post1516002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Ritual or otherwise magic would therefore exist as something separate from them, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27824_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27824\" data-vbnamecard=\"27824\">Arcanus</a> suggested. The idea for using Skinlands memoria is neat, I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think it gives a further dimension, I\u2019d allow Momenti to expand certain Arcanoi by ritualising, but my main aim was to add some ceremony to games, further mystism for the outlawed Guilds etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T04:25:04-07:00","id":1516195,"title":"","content":"Ceremony might be a good descriptor. Rituals work with power from the performer, Rites call on external sources. A ceremony is more like a formalized action to support a technique; for the Shadowlands it would mean utilizing the native building blocks (like Memory, Souls, Pathos etc) in unique ways. Soulforging would be a particular example- and I like the idea that something like that has always been there without anyone paying too much mind to it. It leaves the setting intact.<br /> <br /> For example, a low-level ceremony employing Memory could be:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using a reed from the banks of the River of Death, the Wraith can focus the ambient memoria of a Haunt into a small soulfire from which they can regain Pathos.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> One reed creates a soulfire the size of a small campfire. It burns for a number of hours equal to the Haunt rating. For each hour spent in direct proximity of the soulfire, a Wraith regains one dot of Pathos. The reed is consumed in the process, and the ambient memoria need to accumulate for 24 hours before the same site can be used again. </div> </div> </div>Stuff like this, actions that seem so mundane to the average Wraith, that they hardly pay any attention- but for those with a knack for metaphysics could scale up to the consecration of a Citadel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T01:46:36-07:00","id":1516325,"title":"","content":"Brief coda, one thing I have ignored so far are Artifacts.There are some examples that are pretty interesting in the context of ceremonies:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fetterguard (Level 5 Artifact)</b><br /> <br /> Appearing as nothing more than a small soulsteel box, inside it holds miniature versions of its owner\u2019s Fetters. Each of these must be made by the wraith herself, though whether she does it through the forge, through Moliate, or through putting together bits and bobs she recovered in the Underworld makes no difference. As long as these icons remain safe within the box, no harm will come to them in the real world, and even supernatural attempts at damaging them will somehow go awry.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This could easily be interpreted as a ceremony where the Artifact elements are components, and is honestly pretty close to any Ritual you would see with Path sorcery. It's probably possible to create new ceremonies by looking at Artifacts and transferring their mechanics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T02:48:54-07:00","id":1516328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516325#post1516325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could easily be interpreted as a ceremony where the Artifact elements are components, and is honestly pretty close to any Ritual you would see with Path sorcery. It's probably possible to create new ceremonies by looking at Artifacts and transferring their mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a good idea, on a contextual level ceremonial versions could be attempts by Wraiths to emulate artefacts that are generally held by the more powerful or influential.<br /> <br /> Bit of inspiration from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>\u2019s <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe/page4\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...ment-foe/page4</a>, another coveted ceremony could be for fetterless ancient wraiths to visit the Shadowlands for short periods.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T02:57:29-07:00","id":1516329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516195#post1516195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ceremony might be a good descriptor. Rituals work with power from the performer, Rites call on external sources. A ceremony is<br /> Stuff like this, actions that seem so mundane to the average Wraith, that they hardly pay any attention- but for those with a knack for metaphysics could scale up to the consecration of a Citadel.</div> </div> </div> </div>It strikes me that whilst some wraiths might resist or even deny the supernatural (even if confronted with it).<br /> The mixing of newer wraiths with those from ancient peoples could see ceremony\u2019s/Momenti performed often, almost as daily rituals.<br /> <br /> Imagine a Victorian spiritualist confronted with an ancient wraith from pagan or Hellenic times and the fact their rituals influence the dead kingdoms (plasm. Etc), offer shelter, protect fetters etc<br /> <br /> I can see meso-American cultures having a large ceremony culture (<i>D\u00eda de los Muertos</i>\u200b. Etc) to strength links with the living.<br /> <br /> Of course the Hierarchy would likely try and stamp its usage out, to maintain the Dictum Mortum, putting them in the hands of cults, renegade and heretic settlements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-28-2023, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T13:03:45-07:00","id":1516517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516329#post1516329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the Hierarchy would likely try and stamp its usage out, to maintain the Dictum Mortum, putting them in the hands of cults, renegade and heretic settlements.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's multiple parties who would have an interest on keeping such knowledge out of the hands of the general public. I imagine many ceremonies would have been preserved inside the Guilds and would have gotten lost along with the other records during the Breaking, something the game keeps bringing up (dang it once more, no DA: Wraith). The Artificers Guild in particular as the main supplier of Artifacts would not want to have their quasi-monopoly broken by folk ceremonies making their services obsolete, or at least, less necessary.<br /> <br /> The idea of ceremonies that mirror and complement Skinlands Rites for the dead makes <i>so much</i> sense. If you already have the living do all kind customary memorial rites on certain dates, why wouldn't there be a matching counterpart? One party pushes, the other pulls. Much more effective that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:13:51-07:00","id":1516531,"title":"","content":"I would desperately love to get <b>Dark Ages: Wraith</b>, even if only as a Storytellers Vault product \u2014 so long as it's done by someone knowledgeable in Wraith lore. I would not, for example, attempt the project myself, because I don't know enough about Wraith to do it justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:55:01-07:00","id":1516792,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, and you are right that it it is a complicated matter. Not the least of which is the big geographical question of what the Underworld used to be like before the Third Maelstrom created the Tempest and severed Stygia from the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T01:42:50-07:00","id":1516865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516517#post1516517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's multiple parties who would have an interest on keeping such knowledge out of the hands of the general public. I imagine many ceremonies would have been preserved inside the Guilds and would have gotten lost along with the other records during the Breaking, something the game keeps bringing up (dang it once more, no DA: Wraith). The Artificers Guild in particular as the main supplier of Artifacts would not want to have their quasi-monopoly broken by folk ceremonies making their services obsolete, or at least, less necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Massively I can see a lot of opportunities in terms of intrigue and espionage as well as adding mysticism.<br /> <br /> When Wraith first came out I created a variation of Barghasts called Fell Hounds, that were moliated by the Hierarchy to hunt magical things in the underworld. (Mage, Liche etc)<br /> <br /> Perhaps those that practice high level Momenti develop other marks or scent, I had witch hunters searching for these rogues.<br /> <br /> Alternatively I can see other kingdoms being quite open to ceremony\u2019s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516517#post1516517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of ceremonies that mirror and complement Skinlands Rites for the dead makes <i>so much</i> sense. If you already have the living do all kind customary memorial rites on certain dates, why wouldn't there be a matching counterpart? One party pushes, the other pulls. Much more effective that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there\u2019s lots of examples not just the cultural ones, look at the yearly vigil that Houdinis fraternity still observe every year, it would be an excellent way for Puppeteers and Proctors to create push pull ceremonies.<br /> <br /> Plus so many cultures that practice ancestor worship and remembrance, not suggesting every skinlands act is a linked ceremony but it\u2019s a good cover particularly on key festivals for practitioners to enact rituals with there own Underworld ceremony\u2019s.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the prospect of cultists and spectres using dark ceremonies to weaken the shroud, open more Nihils etc, so stories could just as readily be centred on stopping a ceremony (on either side).<br /> <br /> In Werewolf the Mexico City Bone Gnawers enacted a ritual to strengthen the Shroud, possibly to keep Spectres contained on the Days of the Dead.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve raised a good point around lost lore during the Breaking an interesting idea would be braving the Tempest to try to find a place that was once part of the unified underworld or perhaps the place has been pushed into the skinlands or exists as one of those haunts that only materialises on certain dates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T01:52:24-07:00","id":1516867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516865#post1516865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Wraith first came out I created a variation of Barghasts called Fell Hounds, that were moliated by the Hierarchy to hunt magical things in the underworld. (Mage, Liche etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>Avoiding triggering the dreaded spam filter by editing.<br /> <br /> Meant to add Fell Hounds are Moliated psychics and possibly sorcerors, my headcanon was that Mage who became Wraiths were generally feared (despite having lost their awakened power) simply because of their knowledge, so the Hierarchy (and probably the Dark Empire of Jade) wouldn\u2019t run the risk of moliating a discovered Mage.<br /> <br /> In the other hand dead Mage and sorcerors would be great candidates for the creation of ceremonies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T03:17:01-07:00","id":1516959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515936#post1515936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine ancient Hellenic Wraiths experimenting with Orphic rituals, later Catholism, Voudoon etc, with the concept of Fetters, Relics etc the concept of drawing power from skinlands memorial seems very in keeping with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516517#post1516517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine many ceremonies would have been preserved inside the Guilds</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a canonical link here I did not see before reading up on the Guilds for the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1516811-wraith-dark-ages-history?p=1516894#post1516894\">Dark Ages thread</a>: Classical period mystery cults (Orphic, Eleusinian, Dionysian etc) are exactly the type of groups that would form the <i>collegia </i>and later consolidate into the Guilds. That would mark another point of the possible loss of ceremonies when jealously guarded secrets fell victim to the War of Guilds, and a budging Guild was destroyed or slandered out of existence. It also fits as this is a specific thing for the Dark Kingdom of Iron and contrasts it from other cultures where ceremonial links between Quick and Dead are still stronger, as you mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1516865#post1516865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s also the prospect of cultists and spectres using dark ceremonies to weaken the shroud, open more Nihils etc, so stories could just as readily be centred on stopping a ceremony (on either side).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Dark Arcanoi tend to be mirrors of the regular Arcanoi, I think it is reasonable to assume that dark ceremonies would follow the same pattern and employ the Shadow counterparts of the building blocks used in regular ones, ie Oblivion instead of Memory, Dark Passions, Angst and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T04:41:54-07:00","id":1539744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld?p=1515641#post1515641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fundamentally, the Underworld is composed of memories.<br /> To preform magic, you have to be &quot;whole&quot;<br /> A Wraith of a Vampire don't have disciplines, because she is missing parts of her Being - but as soon as it became a Risen, Disciplines i na limited form, allowed, may learn Celerity, Fortitude, Obfuscate, and Potence. The Kuei-jin are a special branch of the Risen in a sense, since their creation requires every part of the being to reunite, while a &quot;common&quot; risen needs first of all a Conduit, to store and lock away its Shadow, so incomplete still - more complate than before, but still missing parts, so this limits the potential abilites<br /> <br /> Entities like the Innocent of the Mokol\u00e9 are wraiths, never been able to dream their Archid shape, but the connection to the mnesis allows them to steal, devour, corrupt or alter Memories, but themselves are while spirits in a sense, have Arcanoi<br /> <br /> I would say, as long as you are &quot;whole&quot;, you will be able to prefrom magic... any kind</div> </div> </div> </div>your message made me think a lot, I find the theory very interesting because I never thought that the wraith were not in the continuity of the character's soul, and I admit that I quite like the option , but I can't manage to check all the boxes.<br /> <br /> - if the wraith do not have a soul, they are not integrated into the Wheel.<br /> - if the Underworld is not in the Wheel, why are the Euthanatos so interested in being immersed in the shadowlands for their initiation? what are their goals with regard to the wraith? Do they start from the principle that in the Underworld it is also necessary to help the wraith in difficulty and detect the servants of corruption (Oblivion)?<br /> - if the wraith do not have souls, and the Underworld is part of the Umbra, can we say that all spirits born from the Umbra do not have souls, that the is the soul linked to the Avatar and the Wheel and that the Umbra is astral/etheric/dreamlike? if so, why do the Spheres have their kingdom there, and why do the mages take refuge there?<br /> <br /> Your answer completely changes my vision of the World of Darkness, it's interesting but dizzying (at least for me who is just starting my Mage GMing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28494,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28494-tnntwister","user":"tnntwister","date":". 08-03-2024, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28494-tnntwister","name":"tnntwister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T11:08:39-07:00","id":1540717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1515451-magic-in-the-underworld#post1515451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems to indicate one of two things: Either Wraiths can not work magic, or Arcanoi <i>are</i> magic under a different name.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly it. Arcanoi are not like Vampiric Disciplines, which are in a manner just an extension on the vampiric curse. Arcanoi are not extensions of the Ghost-ic condition, but rather a form of Magic that shapes the &quot;physics&quot; of the Underworld<br /> <br /> Edit: oh yes, now I understand what you meant about &quot;magic&quot;. Yeah, I would agree that Arcanoi are indeed more like a &quot;Science&quot; than &quot;Magic&quot;, but Arcanoi still aren't &quot;inherent abilities&quot; like Disciplines. But yes, I would say that &quot;Science&quot; would be the best way to describe them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 08-21-2024, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}